  been the source of tons of speculation  and theorizing because of the eye  present on the part that covers up  midna's eye it looks almost exactly like  the majora's mascara prompting many  people to believe many different things  about its origin however if you flip the  helmet over you can actually see another  symbol on its back and this one is  pretty clearly the sheikah symbol  complete with those signature three  eyelash thingies anyone who's anyone in  the zelda theory realm knows that  symbology is extremely important to the  series as far as understanding what the  hell is going on so for the sheikah  symbol to pop up here pretty much  confirms that the shika had something to  do with the fused shadow's creation i  wonder what it could be number eight is  that for an iconic weapon that's very  closely associated with the series and  the character of link himself the true  master sword has actually only appeared  in fewer than half of all the zelda  titles out there even though link  himself appears in all of them and i  specify the true master sword because  there are some appearances in the series  that feature not the master sword itself  but rather swords that link uses  becoming as powerful as the master sword  and subsequently being referred to as  just the master sword the true actual  legitimate master sword only appears in  games that follow a specific pattern and  that pattern is ganon no not my dog the  other ganon and if you want it to be  technical it would be to eliminate  demise or the curse of demise's demon  tribe or perhaps to even fight against  the power of the triforce of power but  the point still stands that the master  sword only shows up in games where link  is fighting against ganondorf ganon or  demise which is less than half of them  this means that the sword has a specific  purpose and would rather not be used for  just regular you know pot smashing and  the like and it gives credence to this  text from breath of the wild conce